<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bormida</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bormida is a river of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> that rises in the Ligurian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apennines">Apennines</a> and flows north through southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a>. It joins the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanaro">Tanaro</a> just east of Alessandria, a city founded in 1168 at the meeting of the two rivers. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-marengo">Battle of Marengo</a> of 1800 was fought on the plain beside the Bormida near Alessandria.</p></div>
